## Ki-Rin

A Ki-Rin is a divine beast, long-bodied and scaled: chitinous plates laid over a deer's frame, hooves, and a mouth of carnivorous teeth that slobbers gore. It breathes a rush of divine fire that can turn a crowd to ash, and calls up a deflecting wind to turn aside a blow.

The creature wears an aura of peace, and meeting its eyes shows an intelligence there that a person cannot bring themselves to snuff out. Those caught by it will not raise a hand against it while it lasts. It is no less deadly for that gentleness: one gored a guest to death on the Providence banquet floor, and another turned its fire on the guests after it was taken by mind magic.

Some came through a tear in the [[Phenomena/Weave|weave]] that opened over the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]]'s dance floor.

## Aether Host

An aether host is a celestial pulled through the firmament and bound into a mortal body. The rite does not break the barrier between worlds; it projects the thing's essence through, so the celestial wears a living body as a vessel. The followers of [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Herald|Herald]] in [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence/Tali|Tali]] worked it from a book whose words are not words, and reading that book pulls a reader down into it.

An aether host stands wreathed in a shell of fire. It drinks the life out of those it touches to mend its own wounds, and where no one is within reach it takes to the air and calls down a chain of lightning. Its will is too strong to turn. One was made in the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence/Chapel of the Six|Chapel of the Six]] when [[People/Galzu|Galzu]]'s rite was cut short; [[People/Egan Arithmites|Egan]] put a bullet through its eye and it stopped glowing and fell.
